# Ghostty configuration.
#
# Lives at the XDG path rather than
# ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config.ghostty because
# Ghostty reads both on macOS and only this one on Linux. Note it MERGES the
# two when both exist, so keep only this one.
#
# TERMINAL APPEARANCE ONLY -- with one deliberate exception below. The
# shell itself -- prompt, history, aliases, completion, secrets -- is
# global: every terminal and SSH session reads ~/.zshrc and ~/.zprofile.
# Nothing shell-related is SET here, so there is exactly one obvious
# place to change the shell: the dotfiles repo's dot_zshrc.
#
{{ $a := output (joinPath .chezmoi.sourceDir "scripts" "ghostty-theme.py") "appearance" | trim | fromJson -}}
# The theme names and the light/dark mode are not set here at all: they come
# from settings.toml at the repo root (the appearance settings -- browse the names with
# `ghostty +list-themes`). theme = "system" renders the light:/dark: pair
# Ghostty auto-switches with the OS; "light"/"dark" pin one theme for the
# whole stack. The rest of the stack follows the same signal: the zsh prompt
# uses indexed colors 0-15, Neovim sets 'background' via
# lua/bruce/core/appearance.lua, and delta-theme (~/.local/bin, wired into
# git and lazygit) picks the matching syntax theme.
theme = {{ if eq $a.mode "system" -}}
light:{{ $a.light_theme }},dark:{{ $a.dark_theme }}
{{- else if eq $a.mode "light" -}}
{{ $a.light_theme }}
{{- else -}}
{{ $a.dark_theme }}
{{- end }}

# The one exception to appearance-only: remap Option+Enter to the exact
# byte sequence the Kitty keyboard protocol would send for it anyway
# (esc [ 13 ; 3 u). Kitty-aware apps like pi already receive Option+Enter
# as those bytes, so this changes nothing for them; legacy apps like zsh
# normally get a bare carriage return -- indistinguishable from Enter --
# and this gives ~/.zshrc a byte-distinct key to bind (it runs the
# autosuggestion as-is; esc+cr stays free for Option+Shift+Enter to
# accept without running). No terminal-side fallback is lost: in
# terminals without this remap both chords collapse to esc+cr, which
# ~/.zshrc binds to the safe action (accept, never run).
keybind = opt+enter=text:\x1b[13;3u
